course: dictionary
lesson: 11075
title: Weld: joining metal and people
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To weld means to join two pieces of metal by heating them until they melt and stick together. The place where they are joined is also called a weld.
explain: «In a car factory, big robot arms weld and paint the same way thousands of times without getting tired or bored.» Here weld is a doing word, a verb: the robot arms are joining the metal.
explain: «Robot arms join the steel pieces with several thousand spot welds.» Here weld is a naming word, a noun: a spot weld is one joint. Check the words around it to see which kind of word it is.
fact: Weld is a verb (to weld, welds, welded, welding) and a noun (a weld, welds).
fact: «Weld» means to join pieces of metal by heating them until they melt and stick.
fact: «Weld» can also mean to join people or things closely, as in «welded together».
fact: Welders wear masks to protect their eyes from the bright light.
fact: «Welding light can hurt eyes, so welding happens behind screens.»
exercise: «In a car factory, big robot arms weld and paint the same way thousands of times.» What does weld mean here? | *To join pieces of metal by heating them until they stick | To paint the metal a bright colour | To cut the metal into small pieces | To count the robots
exercise: «Robot arms join the steel pieces with several thousand spot welds.» In this sentence, what is a weld? | *A joint where two pieces of metal have been stuck together | A big factory building | A loud noise | A kind of robot arm
exercise: Welders wear masks. What is the mask for? | *To protect their eyes from the bright light | To make them look like robots | To keep their voices quiet | To stop their hair getting wet
test: «The two bars were welded together so they could not come apart.» What does welded together mean here? | Sawn into small parts | *Joined firmly, so they stick as one piece | Painted in bright colours | Sold to a shop
test: Which sentence uses weld as a noun? | «Welding can be dangerous if you are careless.» | «The robot will weld the door shut.» | «The welder is wearing a mask.» | *«The weld on the door is strong and neat.»
exam: «Most real robots work in factories, warehouses, hospitals and homes; films exaggerate.» What does exaggerate mean? | To paint something a bright colour | *To make something seem bigger or more than it really is | To make something smaller and quieter | To hide something from view
